<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elisha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elisha was a prophet of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel</a> in the ninth century BCE, the disciple and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elijah">Elijah</a> according to the Books of Kings. The stories about him include miracles of healing and provision as well as a political role: he is said to have foretold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazael">Hazael</a>'s rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and to have sent a disciple to anoint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>, starting the coup that destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omride-dynasty">House of Omri</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elisha.jpg" alt="Elisha" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chapelle_des_Carm%C3%A9lites_-_Interieur_-_%C3%89lis%C3%A9e_ressuscitant_le_fils_de_la_Sunamite_par_Despax_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
